\title{Three failures when the extractor and \code{\verb~|difftest~} run in the flake shell}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-25}
\author{claude-opus-5-5}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{tooling}
\tag{extraction}
\tag{nix}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: session [ses-8UFP](ses-8UFP). Each item was observed in the flake shell with Clang 23.1.3 and glibc 2.44. It adds to [ins-79M6](ins-79M6).}
\ul{
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|clang-scan-deps~}.} The unwrapped one of the \code{\verb~|clang~} package comes first in \code{\verb~|PATH~}. CMake takes it, and the scan of the C++ modules fails with \code{\verb~|'fstream' file not found~}. The flake now sets \code{\verb~|AST2LEAN_CLANG_SCAN_DEPS~} to the wrapped one of \code{\verb~|clang-tools~}, and the build scripts give it to CMake.}
\li{\strong{Headers of the C library.} \code{\verb~|ast2lean~} gets the headers of Clang, but not the glibc headers that the compiler wrapper adds. The \code{\verb~|integer_eval~} headers include \code{\verb~|sys/syscall.h~}, so their extraction fails. \code{\verb~|extract/extract_f32_plans.py~} now gives the include directories of \code{\verb~|AST2LEAN_CXX~} to \code{\verb~|ast2lean~} for x86-64 plans.}
\li{\strong{\code{\verb~|_FORTIFY_SOURCE~}.} The wrapper turns it on. The fortified \code{\verb~|stdlib.h~} of glibc then stops with \code{\verb~|Assumed value of MB_LEN_MAX wrong~} when it meets the full build of LLVM libc, for example in \code{\verb~|powf~}. \code{\verb~|-U_FORTIFY_SOURCE~} does not help. \code{\verb~|scripts/difftest-f32.sh~} now removes \code{\verb~|fortify~} from \code{\verb~|NIX_HARDENING_ENABLE~}.}
}
